OPENSTEP binary nib regression tests
===================================

Regenerate the checked-in, original fixtures:
  python3 make-openstep-fixtures.py

When linking against a newly built GUI library, build openstep.m with the
usual GNUstep test flags and private Source/ include path.  Run:
  ./openstep OpenStepFixtures
  ./openstep OpenStepFixtures --gui

The first run does not need a graphical backend.  The second does; windows
are created without ordering them on screen and are closed after checking
outlets, actions, ownership and geometry.  XML plist parsing failures from an
installed base library are reported separately as skips, not binary failures.

From the libs-gui root, a standalone build against installed GUI/base libraries
can exercise the changed loader without rebuilding unrelated GUI files:

  clang $(gnustep-config --objc-flags) -ISource -IHeaders -IHeaders/Additions \
    -DGSNibLoader=GSOpenStepTestNibLoader \
    -DGSXibLoader=GSOpenStepTestXibLoader \
    -DGSGormLoader=GSOpenStepTestGormLoader \
    -DGSGModelLoader=GSOpenStepTestGModelLoader \
    Tests/gui/NSNibLoading/openstep.m Source/GSOpenStepNibReader.m \
    Source/GSOpenStepTypedStream.m \
    Source/GSNibLoader.m Source/GSXibLoader.m Source/GSGormLoader.m \
    Source/GSGModelLoader.m \
    $(gnustep-config --gui-libs) -o /tmp/openstep-tests
  /tmp/openstep-tests Tests/gui/NSNibLoading/OpenStepFixtures --gui

The decoder can be checked independently:
  clang -x objective-c $(gnustep-config --objc-flags) -ISource \
    -fsanitize=address,undefined -g Tests/gui/NSNibLoading/typedstream.c \
    Source/GSOpenStepTypedStream.m $(gnustep-config --base-libs) \
    -o /tmp/typedstream-test
  /tmp/typedstream-test Tests/gui/NSNibLoading/OpenStepFixtures/objects-v4-le.nib

See Source/README.openstep for the design and limits.

Validation on the implementation host (macOS, GNU Objective-C runtime)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
The standalone loader suite and decoder test commands above are the current
regression checks.

Host limitations, independently reproduced:
  - The full GUI build stops in existing NSViewController.m because this
    Objective-C runtime lacks OBJC_ASSOCIATION_ASSIGN.
  - The installed base XML plist parser raises an unrecognized-selector
    exception.  Binary plist loading and XML format probing pass.
  - Enumerating the host's full font collection triggers a GSTimSort assertion
    before nib loading.  GUI tests used FONTCONFIG_FILE pointing at a temporary
    configuration containing only Helvetica; no installed configuration changed.
  - Creating a plain NSMatrix with initWithFrame:mode:cellClass:numberOfRows:
    numberOfColumns: crashes in the installed library without any nib loader.
    Matrix runtime validation could not be completed on this host.

These issues were not worked around by changing GUI element classes.
